Wait, one thing about the `.hud` width: `.game-screen` has `width: fit-content` with align-items: center. The hud has width:100% → 100% of game-screen's content width. game-screen's fit-content width = the max of its children's preferred widths. board-wrap's fit-content = canvas width + 2px border. hud's 100% is circular, but the browser resolves fit-content as the max of the children's max-content sizes; a child with width:100% contributes its content size (the text) — which is small. So game-screen width = max(canvas width, menu text width) = canvas width. And hud's 100% = canvas width.

